course: dictionary
lesson: 7413
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is meant by reading the words around it. «Ruby went to her grandma's in the countryside, where the game would not even load, so she played cards with grandma instead and discovered grandma had the best poker face in the county.» The clues are cards and game, so this poker is a card game.
explain: A poker face is a face that shows no feelings. Nobody can tell if you are happy, worried or bluffing, which means pretending. Grandma kept her face calm, so Ruby could not guess her cards. That is what poker face means in this sentence.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another setting. In an old house, a poker is a metal rod used to move burning wood or coal in a fireplace. Check the clues: a fire means the rod, and cards with players means the game.
explain: Poker the card game is played for money by adults, and betting money is gambling, which is not for children. You can still understand the word by reading the clues. When you are not sure, ask what the words around it are about.
fact: Poker can mean a metal rod used to move burning wood or coal in a fireplace.
fact: Poker can also mean a card game in which players bluff, which means pretend.
fact: A poker face is a face that shows no feelings.
fact: Words with more than one meaning are common, and the clues around them show which meaning is meant.
fact: Poker card games are for adults, and betting money is gambling, which is not for children.
exercise: On a cold night, Dad used the poker to push the logs in the fireplace. What is a poker here? | *A metal rod for moving burning wood or coal | A person who pokes | A kind of face | A card game
exercise: «...grandma had the best poker face in the county.» What does poker face mean? | *A face that shows no feelings | A face made of wood | A face that is always smiling | A face painted with stripes
exercise: Which word in a sentence would show that poker means the card game? | Coal | Fireplace | Logs | *Cards
test: Ben used a poker to stir the coals. What is a poker here? | *Metal rod for moving burning coal | Gambling | Face that shows no feelings | Card game
test: Mia kept a poker face when she lost, so nobody knew she was upset. What does poker face mean? | A face that is always crying | *A face that shows no feelings | A face covered in paint | A face that is hot
exam: A poker is a fire tool, and a poker is also a card game. What does this show about words? | *Some words have more than one meaning, and the context shows which | Words never change their meaning | Every word has only one meaning | Poker is always a card game
